384 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (A popular unsupervised algorithm that partitions data into K clusters, where each data point belongs to the cluster with the nearest mean. Helps in grouping similar summaries to identify which ones might belong to the same session. It is simple, scalable, and efficient for large text embeddings. Works well when clusters are roughly spherical in vector space \(which holds in high-dimensional text data after normalization\). Helps in initializing the reassociation of summaries to sessions, acting as a first-pass grouping.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
