759 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1567 0 R
/E (TF-IDF \(Term Frequency-Inverse Document Frequency\) adjusts word importance based on both intra-document repetition and inter-document relevance.)
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
760 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1568 0 R
/E (Words that appear too frequently within a single summary are down-weighted, preventing redundant or filler terms from dominating the embedding vector.)
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
761 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1569 0 R
/E (This is particularly useful in student-generated summaries: a student with low retention might repeat basic words to artificially extend the summary. TF-IDF corrects this by reducing the weight of those frequently repeated terms.)
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
